{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The checkout is done. Now let me examine the diff to understand the current implementation and the race condition described in the verdict:\n\n\"All log links now share one #log-drawer-body swap target with no hx-sync/abort or request-sequence guard. handleLogs can block up to refreshTimeout (30s), so opening run A then run B before A returns can let A's slower response arrive last and overwrite B in the drawer, showing the wrong run's log; the previous per-run inline targets did not have this cross-run race. Add request serialization/abort or discard stale responses before swap.\"\n\nLet me look at the relevant files: static/canopy.js, templates/log.html, templates/page.html, templates/instance.html, and the server side handleLogs.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The checkout is done. Now let me examine the diff to understand the current implementation and the race condition described in the verdict:\\n\\n\\\"All log links now share one #log-drawer-body swap target with no hx-sync/abort or request-sequence guard. handleLogs can block up to refreshTimeout (30s), so opening run A then run B before A returns can let A's slower response arrive last and overwrite B in the drawer, showing the wrong run's log; the previous per-run inline targets did not have this cross-run race. Add request serialization/abort or discard stale responses before swap.\\\"\\n\\nLet me look at the relevant files: static/canopy.js, templates/log.html, templates/page.html, templates/instance.html, and the server side handleLogs.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me examine the current implementation to understand the race condition described in the Verdict."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ae8b308136a44aa3b0e0596b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788550107325557414-f