ting element.\n\nLet me actually check the vendored htmx source to be precise. There's a vendored htmx.min.js in static/.\n\nActually, rather than relying on my recollection of hx-sync mechanics, the robust and verifiable approach is the JS event-based fix in canopy.js:\n1. Track the requesting element / run id per log request.\n2. On a new log request (`htmx:beforeRequest` with `data-log-open` elt), abort any previous in-flight log request.\n3. Guard the swap: on `htmx:beforeSwap`, if the response belongs to a run different from the currently open one, cancel the swap.\n\nActually, let me look at htmx's API in the vendored version to confirm `htmx.trigger` and `htmx:abort` and `htmx:beforeSwap` use `event.detail.shouldSwap` / `event.preventDefault()`.\n\nLet me check the vendored htmx.min.js. Also let me check the server's handleLogs to understand the refreshTimeout blocking behavior.\n\nLet me read the relevant server code and vendored htmx first.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now I understand the current implementation. Let me confirm the details:\\n\\n1. In `instance.html`, each run's \\\"open log\\\" link has `data-log-open`, `hx-get=\\\"/logs?instance=...&run=...\\\"`, `hx-target=\\\"#log-drawer-body\\\"`, `hx-swap=\\\"innerHTML\\\"`.\\n2. `page.html` has the `#log-drawer` panel with `#log-drawer-body`.\\n3. `canopy.js`'s `openDrawer` sets `content.innerHTML = '<p class=\\\"muted\\\">Loading log…</p>'` and shows the panel.\\n4. There's no `hx-sync`, no `hx-indicator` per request, and no request sequence guard. If the user opens run A then run B before A's response returns, A's slower response can arrive last and overwrite B's content in the drawer.\\n\\nThe verdict says: \\\"Add request serialization/abort or discard stale responses before swap.\\\"\\n\\nSo I need a fix. Options:\\n1. Use `hx-sync` to serialize requests from the log links — e.g., add `hx-sync=\\\"this:replace\\\"` or place an `hx-sync=\\\"#log-drawer-body:repla