"htmx:beforeSwap\\\", m)) return;     // dispatched on r (swap target)\\n```\\n\\nAnd `ae` sets `n.elt = e` where e is the dispatch element. So for `htmx:beforeSwap`, `detail.elt` = `r` = swap target (#log-drawer-body), NOT the link.\\n\\nHold on — BUT also look at the second dispatch in `ae`:\\n```js\\nlet o = e.dispatchEvent(r);   // r = the event, dispatched on e (the dispatch elt)\\nconst i = Bt(t);              // Bt = getEventName? For \\\"htmx:beforeSwap\\\" maybe returns \\\"htmx:beforeSwap\\\"...\\nif (o && i !== t) {\\n  const s = Xt(i, r.detail);  // Xt = makeEvent(name, detail)\\n  o = o && e.dispatchEvent(s); // dispatch on e again with renamed event\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThat's the htmx:beforeSwap → htmx:beforeSwapWith... no wait — Bt is probably event name mapping for prefixed events like \\\"hx-...\\\" Honestly, irrelevant.\\n\\nSo the KEY question: is `detail.elt` the requesting link or the target for beforeSwap in this vendored version?\\n\\nFrom the code: `ae(r, \\\"htmx:beforeSwap\\\", m)` — `r` = `e.target` at that point. So `detail.elt` = swap target element (#log-drawer-body). Hmm — htmx 2.x docs say beforeSwap detail includes `elt` — the element making the request... but in THIS vendored version, the dispatch target is `r = e.target`, and `ae` sets `detail.elt = dispatch element` = target. Hmm wait, let me double check: `let r = e.target;` — hmm, actually, wait. Is `e.target` the swap target `c`? T = `{xhr: g, target: c, requestConfig: C, ...}` — yes, `e.target` = `c` (the resolved swap target). Later `if (u.target) { e.target = Un(t, u.target) }` — server HX-Retarget overrides. So `r` = swap target.\\n\\nTherefore `htmx:beforeSwap` in this vendored htmx dispatches on the swap target with `detail.elt` = swap target, and `detail.target` also = the (possibly updated) swap target. The REQUESTING element is available as... `e.requestConfig`? `C` (requestConfig) contains `elt: r`? Let me check: `const C = {boosted: $, useUrlParams: E, formData: w, parame