rary? No jsdom. But I can write a minimal DOM stub to simulate the critical logic paths (openDrawer abort + beforeSwap guard) with htmx.min.js loaded... loading htmx requires document/window; a stub would be substantial but let me consider a lighter approach: extract and unit-test the pure functions.\\n\\nActually, let me test the core decision logic standalone. I can simulate the guard behavior with a tiny harness that emulates the relevant parts: an element with getAttribute and closest. Let me write a quick node test that loads canopy.js in a minimal fake DOM and exercises:\\n\\n1. Click handling → openDrawer sets lastRun and aborts previous.\\n2. beforeSwap with requestConfig.elt for run A when lastRun=B → preventDefault called.\\n3. beforeSwap for run A when lastRun=A → not prevented.\\n\\nThe canopy.js is wrapped in an IIFE relying on document, window, navigator, htmx... A minimal shim: document with addEventListener, getElementById returning fake elements with querySelector/focus etc. This is doable but the click handler uses event.target.closest... Let me build a small harness. This would be strong evidence for the fix.\\n\\nLet me write /tmp/harness.js:\\n\\n```js\\n// minimal DOM shim\\nfunction makeElt(id, attrs) {\\n  var el = {\\n    id: id,\\n    attrs: attrs || {},\\n    hidden: false,\\n    innerHTML: '',\\n    children: [],\\n    parent: null,\\n    getAttribute: function (k) { return this.attrs[k] !== undefined ? this.attrs[k] : null; },\\n    closest: function (sel) {\\n      var node = this;\\n      while (node) {\\n        if (sel[0] === '#') { if (node.id === sel.slice(1)) return node; }\\n        else if (sel[0] === '[') {\\n          var m = sel.match(/^\\\\[([a-z-]+)\\\\]$/);\\n          if (m && node.attrs && node.attrs[m[1]] !== undefined) return node;\\n        } else if (typeof node.matches === 'function' && node.matches(sel)) return node;\\n        node = node.parent;\\n      }\\n      return null;\\n    },\\n    querySelector: function () { return null; },\\n    querySelectorAll: function () { return []; },\\n    focus: function () {},\\n    addEventListener: function () {},\\n  };\\n  return el;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nHmm — this is getting elaborate. The listeners registered by canopy.js: document.addEventListener(\\\"htmx:beforeSwap\\\"), (\\\"click\\\"), (\\\"keydown\\\"). openDrawer uses drawer(), body(), panel.querySelector(\\\".log-drawer-close\\\") → returns null → skip focus. closeDrawer uses document.contains(lastTrigger) — need document.contains. click handler uses event.target.closest(\\\"[data-log-open]\\\") — target must have closest.\\n\\nLet me write a reasonably complete harness. The key assertions:\\n\\n1. openDrawer(linkB) with a pending previous link lastTrigger=A → calls htmx.trigger(A, \\\"htmx:abort\\\"). I can stub htmx = { trigger: function(elt, ev){ aborted.push([elt, ev]); } }.\\n\\n2. beforeSwap event with requestConfig.elt = linkA while lastRun = B → preventDefault called (discard).\\n\\n3. beforeSwap event with requestConfig.elt = linkB while lastRun = B → preventDefault NOT called.\\n\\n4. beforeSwap with a non-log request elt → not prevented.\\n\\n5. closeDrawer resets lastRun → subsequent beforeSwap for any run → prevented.\\n\\nLet me write this harness carefully. canopy.js expects `window.isSecureContext` etc. only inside copyText — not exercised. `navigator.clipboard` — only in copyLog/copyText — not exercised.\\n\\nStructure of canopy.js IIFE: uses `document`, `window`, `navigator` — globals in node: define `global.document`, `global.window = { setTimeout: setTimeout }`, `global.navigator = {}`. In the IIFE: `window.setTimeout` referenced inside copyLog — not exercised but window must exist as global. `navigator.clipboard` — only in copyText. OK.\\n\\nLet me write the harness and run it with node.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Both checks pass. Now let me build a small Node harness with a minimal DOM shim to empirically verify the guar